# Append-only tables, merged rather than adjudicated.
#
# Every slice in flight appends one row to the end of this file, and git merges
# by line: two branches appending after the same last line conflict on every
# rebase, whatever they actually changed. `union` is git's built-in driver that
# keeps both sides in order instead, which is what resolving one of these by
# hand amounted to.
#
# It never reports a conflict, so it cannot warn about a change that is not an
# append. That is why only this file carries it: `docs/parity.md` and
# `docs/interface-contract.md` are edited in place, and a conflict in those is
# information.
docs/parity-changelog.md merge=union
